#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125668} :activity/id #uuid "55d83791-4999-5136-909d-35e46a8ed919" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050004 :topic/id #uuid "25876b80-efb1-53ed-9327-08d34c32cc9a" :topic/math-academy-id 1903} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125668 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125743 :tutorial/content "To calculate the limit at infinity of a rational function, such as\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\dfrac{x^4}{x^5-x^2}\\right),\n$$\n\n we apply the following procedure:\n\n**Step 1:** Divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the *denominator*.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}-{x}^{2}}) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{4}÷{x}^{5}}{({x}^{5}-{x}^{2})÷{x}^{5}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}}}{\\frac{{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Apply the rule that if $n$ is any positive integer then $\\displaystyle \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{x^n}\\right)=0.$ Evaluate the remaining expression to obtain the answer.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}-{x}^{2}}) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ed558480-81a6-5baf-ab3a-f19468f77d72" :tutorial/math-academy-id 258 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6cb8d91a-6de6-5bd6-878e-78ec12b7fedf" :step/math-academy-id 471 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125669}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125669 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124661 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124392 :question/id #uuid "0fc616fa-c901-53ff-acab-cdada6bb5ce2" :question/math-academy-id "e-80"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048515}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124902} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125082} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314782} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314783} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314789} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329912} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329929} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329933} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329940}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity: Rational Solutions"} :step/id #uuid "eb8b99ee-a21a-5d00-8571-260574714375" :step/math-academy-id 472 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125670}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124662 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124394 :question/id #uuid "b648ed80-e2e1-57c4-bd37-147d92315e90" :question/math-academy-id "e-81"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "020c3de3-bcaf-5ade-ba50-2f15e344157d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049637}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125089} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125146} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314802} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314803} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314804} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335944} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335945} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381881}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity: Infinite Solutions"} :step/id #uuid "98d0d8f6-bd8d-5c4f-811f-469eaac31888" :step/math-academy-id 475 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125671}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125748 :tutorial/content "The horizontal asymptotes of a rational function $y=f(x)$ coincide with the infinite limits of $f(x).$\n\nFor example, we can use the same procedure as before to find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x) = \\dfrac{x+1}{x^2+2}.$ As a result, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})}{(1+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{1+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the horizontal asymptote of the graph $y=f(x)$ is $y=0$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/27/27c77f2d6a06bad338982d000f916811201c45e9b16713caf40cc4d5bcf911bd.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "298d636c-df6c-580c-adce-c09a77dec64a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 261 :tutorial/title "Horizontal Asymptotes of Rational Functions"} :step/id #uuid "22bf77c7-a859-5972-9d3a-30c0590708ed" :step/math-academy-id 477 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124663 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124395 :question/id #uuid "c3798fe4-058f-5970-a903-65c654abb788" :question/math-academy-id "e-82"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049037}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124911} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124919} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243931} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297271} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314805} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314806} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323682} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323718} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323719} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323720} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323723} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381884}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Asymptote of a Rational Function"} :step/id #uuid "f59b9e85-79cc-5fcd-b7a2-da25e2aeac81" :step/math-academy-id 478 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125673}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124664 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124408 :question/id #uuid "32a8e4bb-4191-55a8-883b-baa36f67b061" :question/math-academy-id "e-83"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124920} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124921} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237819} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237820} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243925} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323721} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323722} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335946} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335947} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335948} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348056} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348057}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying When a Rational Function has No Horizontal Asymptote"} :step/id #uuid "f3b88a81-a304-57e3-a798-5432c418d285" :step/math-academy-id 480}] :activity/title "Limits at Infinity and Horizontal Asymptotes of Rational Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124703}]}
